			Apache Kafka

=> Open source API given by Apache 
=> used to implement Message Queue concepts
=> Supports Cluster (multiple Message Brokers)
=> Everything is Topic only. (P2P, Pub/Sub)
=> Data Will be sent in Serialized format and DeSerialized at Consumer.

=> Kafka s/w is called as EcoSystem.

EcoSystem = Zookeeper + Topics + Cluster

Cluster = Multiple Message Brokers as a unit.
 On EcoSystem setup, cluster is created with size 1 (one Message Broker)
 by default. Based on no.of consumers, no.of Message brokers are
 created and allocated to consumer by Zookeeper.

Topics = It is a Memory. Holds data based on topicName and Data Partitions
(index number /offset starts from zero)

Zookeeper = It controls both Cluster and Topics.


===One Topic + One Message Broker Process=======================
1. Producer application is started and reading data from different sources
(FileSystem, Database, Network stream..etc)

2. It is connected with EcoSystema and sending data using KafkaTemplate
  in K=V format.

3. A new topic is created in Kafka S/w if it is not exist.
   Data is stored in packets formats those are called as "Partitions"
   which are noted with index numbers called as "Offset Ids"

4. Data is received from Producer application in Serialized format
	and stored inside Topics Partitions.

5. Consumer application is started and it is giving Key(topicName) to
   EcoSystem. 
   
6.  ZooKeeper allocates Message Broker to Consumer App.

7. Now, Message Broker checks for given topic (Exist or not?)
8. If exist, Message Replica makes a cloned copy of Message(from topic)
9. Message Brokers reads all data partitions clonings.
10. Message will be delivered to Consumer application 
    in Deserilized format.
