Goto Home location inside CMD:
Ex: D:\kafka_2.12-2.8.1

1. Zookeeper
.\bin\windows\zookeeper-server-start.bat .\config\zookeeper.properties

2. Kafka Server/Cluster
.\bin\windows\kafka-server-start.bat .\config\server.properties

3. Create new Topic
.\bin\windows\kafka-topics.bat --create --zookeeper localhost:2181 --replication-factor 1 --partitions 1 --topic testone

4. Producer
.\bin\windows\kafka-console-producer.bat --bootstrap-server localhost:9092 --topic testone

5. Consumer
.\bin\windows\kafka-console-consumer.bat --bootstrap-server localhost:9092 --topic testone --from-beginning
.\bin\windows\kafka-console-consumer.bat --bootstrap-server localhost:9092 --topic sajid --from-beginning
--

6. how to check the topics created
\bin\windows\kafka-topics --list --bootstrap-server localhost:9092

7. how to descibe the topic
.\bin\windows\kafka-topics --describe --topic sajid_topic_1 --bootstrap-server localhost:9092

8. How to check the consumer group
.\bin\windows\kafka-consumer-groups.bat --bootstrap-server localhost:9092 --describe --group mygroup

*) Note:
-> Zookeeper starts at port 2181
-> Full kafka s/w runs at 9092
-> Stop them using ctl+C command 
	in order: Consumer, Producer, Kafka Server and then Zookeeper
